<title>THAILAND: Thai sugar vessel movements on April 23.</title>
<headline>Thai sugar vessel movements on April 23.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Independent surveyors detailed</p>
<p>Thai sugar freight movement as follows (in tonne tel quels):</p>
<p>Vessel		  Position	  Quantity    Destination</p>
<p>Yun Hua		 SLD Apr 18	12,000	Japan</p>
<p>Dibena Happy	  SLD Apr 18	 6,000	Singapore</p>
<p>Solar Glory	   SLD Apr 18	10,000	China</p>
<p>Feng Ge		 SLD Apr 19	12,000	Pakistan</p>
<p>Bismihitala	   N/A		  9,600	Mombasa</p>
<p>Jilin		   ETB Apr 22	11,000	Indonesia</p>
<p>Alam Teladan	  N/A		 16,800	Malaysia</p>
<p>Great Concert	 ETD Apr 25	11,000	Indonesia</p>
<p>Pipob Samut	   N/A		 15,000	Japan</p>
<p>Saint John	    ETR Apr 18	14,000	S.Korea</p>
<p>Ban Ann		 ETA Apr 21	14,100	S.Korea</p>
<p>Sin Hung 2	    ETA Apr 21	12,500	Bangladesh</p>
<p>Hanbonn Brother     ETA Apr 22	13,500	Indonesia</p>
<p>Topaz		   ETA Apr 22	13,350	South Korea</p>
<p>Pitak Samut	   ETB Apr 22	13,000	Japan</p>
<p>Dae Gak Bong	  ETD Apr 22	 8,000	Malaysia</p>
<p>B.U.T II (sub Fuda) ETR Apr 23	 5,000	China</p>
<p>Socolf Lake	   ETA Apr 24	 6,000	Singapore</p>
<p>Bangpo		  ETA Apr 25	 2,000	Indonesia</p>
<p>Chile		   ETA Apr 26	 3,350	Mozambique</p>
<p>Tropical Rose	 ETA Apr 28	 1,500	Cambodia</p>
<p>Alam Teladan	  ETA Apr 28	16,800	Malaysia</p>
<p>Alam Tenaga	   ETA May 01	15,000	Malaysia</p>
<p>Bangbua		 ETA May 01	 5,500	Indonesia</p>
<p>Bangramard	    ETA May 01	 5,500	Indonesia</p>
<p>NOTE: SLD indicates that the vessel has left, ETA =</p>
<p>Estimated Time of Arrival, ETD = Estimated Time of Departure,</p>
<p>ETR = Estimated Time of Readiness, L/CAN indicated period when</p>
<p>vessels are expected in for loading or be cancelled.</p>
